==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From older {{term|lúka|lang=is}}, from {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|lúka|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*lūkaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈljuːka/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|uːka|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|lauk|luku|lokið}}

# {{context|with dative|lang=is}} to [[finish]], to [[end]]
# {{context|with dative|lang=is}} to [[complete]]
# {{context|with dative|lang=is}} to [[end]], to [[close]], to come or bring to an end
# {{context|with dative|lang=is}} [[finalise]]/[[finalize]]
# {{context|with dative|of a|limited period of time|lang=is}} to [[expire]]
# {{context|with dative|lang=is}} to [[conclude]]

